# Revisions of the SDK repositories that mint clones at image build time.
#
# Upstream follows whatever is newest: build/minio-js/install.sh checks out the
# newest tag of minio/minio-js, and build/minio-java/install.sh asks Maven for
# the newest release and checks out the matching tag of minio/minio-java. Two
# builds of the same commit therefore installed different test sources, and a
# patch written against one of them would silently stop applying later.
# Dockerfile.s3s reads the revisions from here instead, so the test sources in
# the image are a function of this repository alone.
#
# The pinned revisions are the versions the archived minio/mint:edge image
# carries (minio-js 8.0.6, minio-java 8.6.0), and that is the point of pinning
# them: upstream has moved on since (8.0.7 and 9.0.3 at the time of writing), and
# building against the newest release would fold an SDK upgrade into the
# comparison between a patched image and the archived one, leaving no way to tell
# which difference came from a patch. When bumping a revision, re-check the patch
# in patches/ that touches the same checkout and repeat the full sweep.
# The values are commit ids, not the annotated tag objects: the install scripts
# check `git rev-parse HEAD` against them, and an annotated tag resolves to a tag
# object rather than to the commit it names.
MINIO_JS_REF=212f2821110e01b0ba5d81b27e11d10fdcb29d7b         # minio/minio-js tag 8.0.6
MINIO_JAVA_REF=f6cfc76769fe9f069acc5b1b52d5eadecee1c0b6       # minio/minio-java tag 8.6.0
# Maven artifact version of MINIO_JAVA_REF. The install script downloads the
# *-all.jar artifacts by version, because Maven publishes no per-commit build.
MINIO_JAVA_VERSION=8.6.0
